proposition.raw:
\label{prop:NU}
Let $W$ be a weighted clone with a positive weighting $\omega\in W$ such that all
operations $f\in\supp(\omega)$ are near-unanimity operations. Then $W$ is crisp.

\label{prop:minority}

Let $W$ be a weighted clone with a positive ternary weighting $\omega\in W$ such that all
operations $f\in\supp(\omega)$ are minority operations. Then $W$ is crisp.

